WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:02.667
-Chelsea Handler, as always,
welcome back to the show.

00:00:02.667 --> 00:00:04.801
-Oh, so happy to be here.
I just love it here.

00:00:04.801 --> 00:00:07.067
-It's good energy, right?
It's good energy out here.

00:00:07.067 --> 00:00:10.167
-Absolutely.
[ Audience cheers ]

00:00:10.167 --> 00:00:12.400
-Congrats, you just had
two sold out shows

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:13.901
at the Beacon here
in New York City.

00:00:13.901 --> 00:00:15.434
-I know. I missed you.
I was hoping you would come,

00:00:15.434 --> 00:00:17.601
but you didn't,
you blew me off, as usual.

00:00:17.601 --> 00:00:19.100
-This is --
No, this is even better

00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:21.067
'cause I'm closer to you here.
-I know. This is --

00:00:21.067 --> 00:00:22.634
That's exactly
what I was thinking.

00:00:22.634 --> 00:00:24.334
-[ Laughs ] I just --
I just wanted

00:00:24.334 --> 00:00:25.634
to see you in person, yeah.

00:00:25.634 --> 00:00:27.300
I can't wait.
I'm gonna check out the tour.

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:29.334
But I wanted to ask you,
if you don't mind --

00:00:29.334 --> 00:00:31.501
I hate doing this
on live television,

00:00:31.501 --> 00:00:33.033
but there are some headlines

00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:35.667
that happened to you
over the summer,

00:00:35.667 --> 00:00:37.734
and I was thinking of maybe
bringing them up and seeing

00:00:37.734 --> 00:00:40.200
if you don't mind, if -- are
they true or what's your story

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:41.734
behind them?
-Yeah, I love headlines. Yeah.

00:00:41.734 --> 00:00:43.734
-I don't know if they're gossip

00:00:43.734 --> 00:00:45.100
or what's going on.
-Right, me neither.

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:46.267
I mean, I can't wait
to hear them.

00:00:46.267 --> 00:00:47.567
Let's start.
-Okay.

00:00:47.567 --> 00:00:49.200
Alright, well, this says,

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:51.467
"Chelsea Handler's
Threesome with Masseuse

00:00:51.467 --> 00:00:53.701
Led to Ted Harbert
Romance End --

00:00:53.701 --> 00:00:55.868
'I Was Very Turned on By' Her".

00:00:55.868 --> 00:00:57.534
[ Laughter ]

00:00:57.534 --> 00:00:59.601
-Okay, well,
I have to tell the truth

00:00:59.601 --> 00:01:01.934
because I'm incapable
of anything else.

00:01:01.934 --> 00:01:06.067
So, that one was tricky because
I did Andy Cohen's radio show,

00:01:06.067 --> 00:01:08.868
and I had -- by the time
I left the studio,

00:01:08.868 --> 00:01:10.400
I had already forgotten
I had done it.

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:12.968
You know what I mean? Like,
we do interviews all the time.

00:01:12.968 --> 00:01:14.367
And during that interview,
he had asked me

00:01:14.367 --> 00:01:15.701
if I had any threesomes.

00:01:15.701 --> 00:01:18.534
And I like to, you know, again,
tell my personal history

00:01:18.534 --> 00:01:21.400
as if it's my own
only personal history.

00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:23.133
And I always forget there
are other people

00:01:23.133 --> 00:01:24.667
involved in my stories.

00:01:24.667 --> 00:01:26.868
So I was walking --
-In this case,

00:01:26.868 --> 00:01:29.334
two other people.
-Yeah. [ Laughs ]

00:01:29.334 --> 00:01:32.567
So I was walking
to lunch the next day,

00:01:32.567 --> 00:01:34.734
and I had a new Apple phone,
and it was blowing up,

00:01:34.734 --> 00:01:36.167
and I couldn't understand
how to work it.

00:01:36.167 --> 00:01:37.968
And I was like,
just stop, stop, stop.

00:01:37.968 --> 00:01:39.934
And then it was a text
from my ex-boyfriend,

00:01:39.934 --> 00:01:42.868
Ted Harbert, who is, you know,
a very dear friend of mine,

00:01:42.868 --> 00:01:46.100
and said, "That was not cool.
Please don't do that again.

00:01:46.100 --> 00:01:48.033
Some things are better
left private."

00:01:48.033 --> 00:01:51.200
And I was like, "Wow,
that's a pretty stern e-mail

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:53.234
to be getting
from my ex-boyfriend."

00:01:53.234 --> 00:01:55.334
And I was like,
"What's he talking about?"

00:01:55.334 --> 00:01:58.033
And then I was like,
"Did I say something?"

00:01:58.033 --> 00:02:02.267
And then I Googled myself,
-Oh, no.

00:02:02.267 --> 00:02:04.200
Don't ever do that.
-And every e-mail was like,

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:07.300
"Chelsea Handler ends --
breaks up with Ted Harbert

00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:09.901
because of masseuse --
threesome with masseuse."

00:02:09.901 --> 00:02:12.534
So I really want to clarify,
I want to go on the record

00:02:12.534 --> 00:02:15.567
that that is not why
our relationship ended.

00:02:16.901 --> 00:02:18.334
[ Laughter ]

00:02:18.334 --> 00:02:19.567
-That's not why?
-No.

00:02:19.567 --> 00:02:21.534
We did have a lot
of threesomes and that --

00:02:21.534 --> 00:02:23.334
while that's private,
it's already out there.

00:02:23.334 --> 00:02:25.434
So I'm gonna double down
on that

00:02:25.434 --> 00:02:27.267
and just say
that we didn't break up

00:02:27.267 --> 00:02:29.000
because I left him for the
masseuse.

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:30.634
That didn't happen.
-You think that's why

00:02:30.634 --> 00:02:33.400
he's upset?
[ Laughter ]

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:35.567
You think that's why he's mad?

00:02:35.567 --> 00:02:37.334
He's saying with a stern e-mail,
he's like,

00:02:37.334 --> 00:02:38.400
"I just want you
to tell the truth.

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:40.634
We had other problems."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:40.634 --> 00:02:43.133
-But you know Ted Harbert.
I thought it gave --

00:02:43.133 --> 00:02:45.868
So many people came up to me --
He was your boss at some point.

00:02:45.868 --> 00:02:47.901
-I know.
-So many people came up to me

00:02:47.901 --> 00:02:49.100
and they were like, "Wow,

00:02:49.100 --> 00:02:51.167
that gave Ted Harbert
a lot of street cred.

00:02:51.167 --> 00:02:53.467
Who knew he was
having threesomes?"

00:02:53.467 --> 00:02:54.734
[ Laughter ]

00:02:54.734 --> 00:02:56.434
So, I just want to say he was.

00:02:56.434 --> 00:02:58.400
-Oh, my gosh, stop saying that.

00:02:58.400 --> 00:02:59.567
[ Laughter ]

00:02:59.567 --> 00:03:01.601
Now I'm getting an e-mail,
by the way.

00:03:01.601 --> 00:03:04.000
-But I love Ted Harbert.
I love you, if you're watching.

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:05.968
Hopefully not.

00:03:05.968 --> 00:03:09.901
-Ted, I love you, too.
We kept it at twosome.

00:03:09.901 --> 00:03:11.734
We kept it at two--
We kept it at two--

00:03:11.734 --> 00:03:12.734
Alright,
how about this headline?

00:03:12.734 --> 00:03:14.234
-We both love you, Ted.

00:03:14.234 --> 00:03:15.767
-We do.
How about this headline?

00:03:15.767 --> 00:03:18.667
"Chelsea Handler Reveals
She Is Dating Mystery Man

00:03:18.667 --> 00:03:21.167
Who Is 'Full of Love
and Positivity'".

00:03:21.167 --> 00:03:23.868
Ooh.
-That was also a mistake.

00:03:23.868 --> 00:03:25.434
That was --
[ Laughter ]

00:03:25.434 --> 00:03:28.200
I posted a photo with my --

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:31.667
Okay, so I have a summer place
that I like to go in Spain,

00:03:31.667 --> 00:03:35.801
and down underneath the house or
below the house, there's a bar.

00:03:35.801 --> 00:03:39.234
And the bartender became
a very close friend of mine

00:03:39.234 --> 00:03:40.868
for obvious reasons.

00:03:40.868 --> 00:03:43.234
And I --
-That bartender's you.

00:03:43.234 --> 00:03:45.100
-Yeah, I mean,
we spent a lot of time together,

00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:47.267
and so he became my baby,
and I called him "baby",

00:03:47.267 --> 00:03:50.200
and we were very affectionate
with each other because --

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:51.400
There he is.
Oh, there he is.

00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:52.801
Look. Look how cute he is.
-"This is my baby.

00:03:52.801 --> 00:03:54.334
He's full of love
and positivity,

00:03:54.334 --> 00:03:57.367
and his body
is my wonderland.

00:03:57.367 --> 00:04:02.133
I love my baby,
and now, I go back to work."

00:04:02.133 --> 00:04:04.267
-That's right.
And so, bye-bye, baby.

00:04:04.267 --> 00:04:06.934
And now baby's famous.
Look at him. Look at baby.

00:04:06.934 --> 00:04:09.234
-So you call him baby,
but not because he's baby.

00:04:09.234 --> 00:04:11.300
He's just...
-Not because he's my baby.

00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:14.934
Because he's -- I love people
who bring drinks to me.

00:04:14.934 --> 00:04:16.801
[ Laughter ]

00:04:16.801 --> 00:04:18.501
Baby, that's --
Then you're my baby.

00:04:18.501 --> 00:04:20.167
-That's a great way --
-Yes.

00:04:20.167 --> 00:04:21.701
-That's a great way
of putting it.

00:04:21.701 --> 00:04:24.300
-It's like, baby, you know.
I kissed him on the lips.

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:25.434
Every time he brought me
a drink, I was like,

00:04:25.434 --> 00:04:28.100
"Mwah, thank you."
You know, just happiness.

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:29.767
Really.
-Happy baby, yeah.

00:04:29.767 --> 00:04:31.367
Can we talk
about the standup tour?

00:04:31.367 --> 00:04:32.634
-Yes.
-It's going through December?

00:04:32.634 --> 00:04:34.167
-I'm coming everywhere,
you guys.

00:04:34.167 --> 00:04:36.234
Because you know what I love?
Standup.

00:04:36.234 --> 00:04:38.133
-You do?
-I do. I love it so much.

00:04:38.133 --> 00:04:39.634
I took a break,
and I came back,

00:04:39.634 --> 00:04:41.634
like, three specials ago
or two specials ago,

00:04:41.634 --> 00:04:42.968
and I just can't
get enough of it.

00:04:42.968 --> 00:04:44.267
So I love --

00:04:44.267 --> 00:04:45.968
I just love performing
and telling my stories.

00:04:45.968 --> 00:04:47.434
They're so ridiculous,
my stories.

00:04:47.434 --> 00:04:48.734
-They're my favorite.
-You know, I mean,

00:04:48.734 --> 00:04:51.100
I have a great story
this time about Andrew Cuomo.

00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:52.801
I almost had
a threesome with him,

00:04:52.801 --> 00:04:54.634
but it didn't quite pan out.
-Oh, it does not --

00:04:54.634 --> 00:04:56.167
You're gonna get in trouble.
-No, I'm not gonna get

00:04:56.167 --> 00:04:58.167
in trouble because it's true.
And --

00:04:58.167 --> 00:05:00.400
Not the threesome.
Not the threesome part.

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:01.701
-That was the part
I'm concerned about.

00:05:01.701 --> 00:05:02.868
-No, no, no.
We didn't have a threesome.

00:05:02.868 --> 00:05:04.267
We didn't even have a twosome,
but I was trying

00:05:04.267 --> 00:05:05.300
to drum up
some business with him.

00:05:05.300 --> 00:05:08.267
Anyway...
[ Laughter ]

00:05:08.267 --> 00:05:10.000
That was when he was,
you know, cool and fun

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:11.300
and, like, leading our nation

00:05:11.300 --> 00:05:13.734
at a time where we were
dehydrated for leadership.

00:05:13.734 --> 00:05:15.300
So... but that didn't
come to fruition.

00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:17.300
But I have some good stories
in my standup

00:05:17.300 --> 00:05:19.567
that it's -- it gives me
a lot of joy to share them

00:05:19.567 --> 00:05:21.501
because the only person
who comes out

00:05:21.501 --> 00:05:23.300
looking really stupid is me,
you know what I mean?

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:25.801
Everybody else
doesn't come out --

00:05:25.801 --> 00:05:27.601
come out looking badly,
I don't think.

00:05:27.601 --> 00:05:29.400
-No. Not at all.
-I don't -- Yeah.

00:05:29.400 --> 00:05:31.434
I mean, look at Ted Harbert.
He's having threesomes,

00:05:31.434 --> 00:05:33.267
you know?
-Stop saying that.

00:05:33.267 --> 00:05:35.367
[ Laughter ]

00:05:35.367 --> 00:05:38.000
-I got rid of my Apple Watch
so he can't text me again.

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:39.167
-I wanted to --

00:05:39.167 --> 00:05:40.567
Since the last time
you've been on the show,

00:05:40.567 --> 00:05:42.801
you guest hosted
on "The Daily Show",

00:05:42.801 --> 00:05:44.767
and I gotta say,
you were phenomenal.

00:05:44.767 --> 00:05:47.334
It was such a great job.
-Oh, thank you. Thank you.

00:05:47.334 --> 00:05:49.234
I loved it.
-People loved it.

00:05:49.234 --> 00:05:50.534
You got great --

00:05:50.534 --> 00:05:51.534
'Cause you know
what you're doing.

00:05:51.534 --> 00:05:53.300
You're smart, you're funny,

00:05:53.300 --> 00:05:54.634
you're quick, you're sharp.

00:05:54.634 --> 00:05:56.100
And it got great headlines.

00:05:56.100 --> 00:05:58.200
And I go,
"This is such a perfect fit."

00:05:58.200 --> 00:06:00.634
And I go, "Man,
when are they making the move?

00:06:00.634 --> 00:06:02.834
When is Chelsea Handler
taking over 'Daily Show'?"

00:06:02.834 --> 00:06:06.300
-Oh, well, what I will say
about that is that I think

00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:09.801
we are in a very important
cultural moment, you know,

00:06:09.801 --> 00:06:11.734
with women dominating culture.

00:06:11.734 --> 00:06:14.601
We have -- Yeah.
-I agree.

00:06:14.601 --> 00:06:16.501
-The two highest grossing tour.

00:06:16.501 --> 00:06:18.367
I mean, look at T--
look at Taylor Swift.

00:06:18.367 --> 00:06:20.434
She's, like, our president now,
you know?

00:06:20.434 --> 00:06:22.501
Like, I'm like, Taylor Swift
is ruling the universe.

00:06:22.501 --> 00:06:24.701
Beyoncé -- the two highest
grossing tours

00:06:24.701 --> 00:06:26.968
of the summer are women.
-Yes.

00:06:26.968 --> 00:06:29.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:29.300 --> 00:06:31.801
-The highest grossing movie
of the year, you know,

00:06:31.801 --> 00:06:33.334
the highest grossing movie
of the year

00:06:33.334 --> 00:06:36.501
was directed by a woman
about women, you know?

00:06:36.501 --> 00:06:38.968
"Barbie".

00:06:38.968 --> 00:06:40.834
And look at --
Like, you look at Coco Gauff

00:06:40.834 --> 00:06:42.701
and how many people
are watching her

00:06:42.701 --> 00:06:45.801
win her very first grand slam
versus watching the man

00:06:45.801 --> 00:06:48.767
who broke every record
and is breaking them,

00:06:48.767 --> 00:06:50.601
And...
-Women.

00:06:50.601 --> 00:06:52.300
-And just --
just the way that women

00:06:52.300 --> 00:06:53.634
are showing up
for each other, you know?

00:06:53.634 --> 00:06:55.133
You look at women's soccer,
it's more watched

00:06:55.133 --> 00:06:56.634
